      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Heutagogy (Self-Determined Learning):** Moving beyond Pedagogy (child-learning) and Andragogy (adult-learning) to study how learners become the primary agents of their own capability.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "topic-set-self-determination-theory-20251127123653.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metacognition & Self-Regulated Learning (SRL):** The specific cognitive strategies (planning, monitoring, evaluating) that operationalize the motivation SDT provides.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 117,
          "source": "topic-set-self-determination-theory-20251127123653.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Networked Learning Theory:** How knowledge is constructed through connections between people and information nodes, complementing the \"Relatedness\" aspect of SDT.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 117,
          "source": "topic-set-self-determination-theory-20251127123653.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Polanyi's Tacit Knowledge:** Understanding that \"we know more than we can tell,\" and how SDT facilitates the confidence to explore uncodified knowledge.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 117,
          "source": "topic-set-self-determination-theory-20251127123653.md"
        }
      ]
